ctric bike","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7945-bcc7-9997c5087ee5","description":"a recumbent bike","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7178-a5a5-ebe3822c4f57","description":"a tandem bike","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7f3d-827a-fd0d698bb360","category":"01a21312-b489-7d12-a39e-857aff280926","question":"In which sport might you encounter the Cyclops system?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Tennis used Cyclops to detect serves that went long; Wimbledon first introduced the system in 1980.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad73-75e2-867a-d87ad42b7b40","description":"Tennis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-77ce-a394-cdf18505a244","description":"Soccer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7d9f-8786-c9ce877bd43c","description":"Badminton","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7f2f-86eb-8ed8a44ec2a8","description":"Volleyball","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7b65-95ca-8004458e573a","category":"01a21312-b489-7d12-a39e-857aff280926","question":"What is the \'perfect score\' in a game of Ten Pin Bowling?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A score of 300 requires 12 consecutive strikes: one in each frame, with two bonus rolls after a strike in the tenth frame.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad73-793b-8738-4021ff59ec3a","description":"300","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-75fb-a53f-43ae2c288ce8","description":"200","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7757-9704-712250e47b8f","description":"330","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7b22-8984-b16d86ae6fbe","description":"240","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad73-7daf-883a-fe505a100970","category":"01a21312-b489-7d12-a39e-857aff280926","question":"To the nearest mile, how many miles are in a marathon?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Rounded to the nearest mile, the distance is 26 miles. The course was extended at the 1908 London Olympics to finish in front of the royal box.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad73-70fe-